  "text": "ordinarium.supplices-te-rogamus",
  "about": "Bowed low, with his joined hands resting on the altar, the priest asks God that the offering be carried by the hands of His holy Angel to the altar on high before the divine majesty. The prayer does not name the Angel. The clause beginning with “ut” leads to “repleámur”: those who receive the Body and Blood of Christ ask to be filled with every blessing and grace.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": { "narrative": "The priest bows low and lays his joined hands upon the altar." },
    "s02": { "translation": "We humbly ask You, almighty God: command that Your holy Angel carry these offerings in his hands to Your altar on high, before Your divine majesty:", "translation_citations": [{ "title": "The Missal for the Use of the Laity (1853)", "locator": "printed pp. 26–27", "url": "https://archive.org/details/missal_for_use_of_laity_1853-f_c_husenbeth" }, { "title": "The Missal for the Laity (1846)", "locator": "printed pp. 67–68", "url": "https://archive.org/details/TheMissalForTheLaity" }, { "title": "The Family Prayer-book (1839)", "locator": "printed p. 92", "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_family_prayer-book,_containing_all_the_public_and_private_devotions_in_use_amongst_English_Catholics._(IA_TheFamilyPrayerBookContaining).pdf" }] },
    "s04": { "translation": "so that all of us who", "translation_citations": [{ "title": "The Missal for the Use of the Laity (1853)", "locator": "printed pp. 26–27", "url": "https://archive.org/details/missal_for_use_of_laity_1853-f_c_husenbeth" }, { "title": "The Missal for the Laity (1846)", "locator": "printed pp. 67–68", "url": "https://archive.org/details/TheMissalForTheLaity" }, { "title": "The Family Prayer-book (1839)", "locator": "printed p. 92", "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_family_prayer-book,_containing_all_the_public_and_private_devotions_in_use_amongst_English_Catholics._(IA_TheFamilyPrayerBookContaining).pdf" }] },
    "s03": { "narrative": "The priest kisses the altar." },
    "s11": { "translation": "through this participation at the altar", "translation_citations": [{ "title": "The Missal for the Use of the Laity (1853)", "locator": "printed pp. 26–27", "url": "https://archive.org/details/missal_for_use_of_laity_1853-f_c_husenbeth" }, { "title": "The Missal for the Laity (1846)", "locator": "printed pp. 67–68", "url": "https://archive.org/details/TheMissalForTheLaity" }, { "title": "The Family Prayer-book (1839)", "locator": "printed p. 92", "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_family_prayer-book,_containing_all_the_public_and_private_devotions_in_use_amongst_English_Catholics._(IA_TheFamilyPrayerBookContaining).pdf" }] },
    "s05": { "narrative": "The priest joins his hands and makes the sign of the cross once over the Host and once over the chalice." },
    "s06": { "translation": "shall receive the most holy Body and Blood of Your Son,", "translation_citations": [{ "title": "The Missal for the Use of the Laity (1853)", "locator": "printed pp. 26–27", "url": "https://archive.org/details/missal_for_use_of_laity_1853-f_c_husenbeth" }, { "title": "The Missal for the Laity (1846)", "locator": "printed pp. 67–68", "url": "https://archive.org/details/TheMissalForTheLaity" }, { "title": "The Family Prayer-book (1839)", "locator": "printed p. 92", "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_family_prayer-book,_containing_all_the_public_and_private_devotions_in_use_amongst_English_Catholics._(IA_TheFamilyPrayerBookContaining).pdf" }] },
    "s07": { "narrative": "The priest signs himself." },
    "s08": { "translation": "may be filled with every heavenly blessing and grace.", "translation_citations": [{ "title": "The Missal for the Use of the Laity (1853)", "locator": "printed pp. 26–27", "url": "https://archive.org/details/missal_for_use_of_laity_1853-f_c_husenbeth" }, { "title": "The Missal for the Laity (1846)", "locator": "printed pp. 67–68", "url": "https://archive.org/details/TheMissalForTheLaity" }, { "title": "The Family Prayer-book (1839)", "locator": "printed p. 92", "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_family_prayer-book,_containing_all_the_public_and_private_devotions_in_use_amongst_English_Catholics._(IA_TheFamilyPrayerBookContaining).pdf" }] },
    "s09": { "narrative": "The priest joins his hands." },
    "s10": { "translation": "Through the same Christ our Lord. Amen.", "translation_citations": [{ "title": "The Missal for the Use of the Laity (1853)", "locator": "printed pp. 26–27", "url": "https://archive.org/details/missal_for_use_of_laity_1853-f_c_husenbeth" }, { "title": "The Missal for the Laity (1846)", "locator": "printed pp. 67–68", "url": "https://archive.org/details/TheMissalForTheLaity" }, { "title": "The Family Prayer-book (1839)", "locator": "printed p. 92", "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_family_prayer-book,_containing_all_the_public_and_private_devotions_in_use_amongst_English_Catholics._(IA_TheFamilyPrayerBookContaining).pdf" }] }
  },
